    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0246",
      "sequence": 258,
      "meaning": "The sensible kings warn the boasters not to die pointlessly through empty talk: imagined sweets do not still hunger. They advise them to recognize Sītā as the Mother of the world and Raghupati as its Father, and to feast their eyes upon the beautiful, joy-giving brothers, abodes of every virtue and dwelling in Śiva’s heart. Why leave an ocean of nectar nearby and run toward a mirage to die? Let each go wherever inclination leads; they themselves have gained the fruit of birth today. Speaking thus, the good kings lovingly contemplate the matchless forms. From aerial cars the gods watch, shower flowers and sing. Knowing the right moment, Janaka summons Sītā, and her clever, beautiful companions respectfully escort her.",
