    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0248",
      "sequence": 260,
      "meaning": "Sītā goes with her wise companions as they sing in enchanting voices. A beautiful new sari graces her youthful body; the incomparable Mother of the world bears immense splendour. Every ornament is handsome and well placed, arranged by her friends upon each limb. When Sītā steps into the arena, men and women are bewitched by her form; gods joyfully sound kettledrums, shower blossoms, and celestial dancers sing. The victory garland shines in her lotus hand. She suddenly glances at all the kings, who fall under delusion; then, startled, she seeks Rāma and sees the brothers near the sage, her eager eyes finding their treasure. Bashful before elders and the vast assembly, Sītā appears to look toward her companions while bringing Raghubīra into her heart.",
