    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0250",
      "sequence": 262,
      "meaning": "The heralds proclaim that Śiva’s immensely heavy and hard bow is Rāhu to the moon of royal arm-strength, as everyone knows: even the great champions Rāvaṇa and Bāṇa looked upon it and departed. Whoever in today’s royal assembly breaks that stern bow of Tripurāri will win all three worlds together with Vaidehī, who will choose him without further deliberation. Hearing the vow, every king becomes eager; swollen with a warrior’s pride, they fasten their gear, bow to their chosen gods and rise impatiently. Striding up fiercely, they seize Śiva’s bow again and again, but it will not lift despite a million exertions. Those with some judgment do not approach it. Foolish kings grasp at it furiously, then retreat in shame as though, upon receiving their strength, the bow only grows heavier.",
